  message: "CLOSED done, 2026-09-25 (P2 review, dev e4a47383ab). Fixed AFTER this row's last note. The 2026-09-24T07:12Z note records the row as \"WRONG row that is KEPT ... Blocked by WI-bakik\". WI-bakik then landed the same day: 00c5097aaf (2026-09-24 16:24 -0400, \"fix(python catalogue): enumerate urllib.request, then drop the false Request send row (WI-bakik)\").\n\nEVIDENCE:\n- Production loader: `load_catalog('python')` lists no urllib.request.Request row under any boundary. urllib.request's rows are urlopen / urlretrieve / ftpwrapper (net_send), urlcleanup (fs_write), and the env_read / net_recv helpers. python.yaml:575 records why: \"`Request` is NOT here: it builds a request object and sends nothing, and `urlopen(req)` is the send\".\n- The blocker the row named is gone. python.yaml carries `module: urllib.request.Request, completeness: complete` (retrieved 2026-09-14), so an unrowed Request(...) call no longer withholds clean verdicts.\n- Live repro of the row's shape: a.py with `req = Request(u); req.add_header(...); return urlopen(req)`, full survey, then `hypergumbo io-boundaries --format json`. Only net_send chains to `urllib.request.urlopen` appear, and none for Request. The attribution now sits at the call that crosses, per ADR-0049 ruling 1.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: the erlang io_lib:format sibling named in the title's \"same shape\" was not re-checked here. The same fixture yields TWO identical urlopen chains; that looks like the import-edge-as-I/O-chain shape recorded on WI-pimun today, not this row's defect."  # 42cb
